  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING LOCAL CAPACITY FOR GIBBON CONSERVATION IN CAMBODIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to (1) strengthen capacities of local teachers and community members to deliver environmental education in rural communities in gibbon habitat to reduce consumer demand for gibbons as illegal pets and the risk of human-ape conflicts; (2) strengthen the capacity of the Chi Phat Community Anti-Poaching Unit (CAPU) to enforce in-situ protection of critical pileated gibbon habitat in the Cardamom Mountains. This enhanced capacity includes providing patrol teams with necessary field gear, support to pick up snares across nearly 9,000km over the three years, help CAPU coordinate their patrol efforts with Forest Ranger Teams, implement an improved CAPU patrol management system, including a new excel database for tracking and analyzing patrol results, and train CAPU leaders to use the new excel database to manage patrol data; and (3) conduct applied research through monitoring and management of the reintroduced pileated gibbon population in Angkor Archeological Park to support the growing population and address any human-ape conflicts that arise.</narrative>
  </description>
